      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1854 the Central of Georgia Railway from Savannah met the Georgia Railroad from Augusta at Millen, sparking its growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millen%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Named after McPherson B., Millen became known as “Millen’s Junction” when it was chartered in 1881.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.georgiaencyclopedia.org/articles/counties-cities-neighborhoods/millen/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Millen serves as the county seat of Jenkins County, where a courthouse was erected in 1910.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
